ut he did say  i have tremendous respect for wesley as  an actor he used to be a friend we're  not friends anymore i don't think anyone  involved in that film had a good  experience certainly i didn't  2000's charlie's angels was a box office  hit bolstered by a star-studded cast  that included cameron diaz drew  barrymore and lucy as the angels and  bill murray as the pseudo-manager bosley  however in reality the team didn't seem  as connected as they did in the movie  the story goes that there was a rewrite  of one scene and murray wasn't happy  with it for some reason he took his  frustration out on lou despite her  claiming not to have anything to do with  the changes she addressed the incident  during an interview on the los angeles  times podcast asian enough according to  lou murray began insulting her and she  didn't back down she said i stood up for  myself and i don't regret it because no  matter how low on the totem pole you may  be or wherever you came from there's no  need to condescend or put other people  down the two have seemingly rekindled  their professional relationship but lou  still thinks she did the right thing in  standing up to murray  it's hard to pinpoint the exact reason  for the long-standing feud between sex  and the city co-stars sarah jessica  parker and kim cattrall but it's clear  that the two weren't the best of friends  on set in an interview with piers morgan  cottrell explained why she didn't want  to return for the reboot series saying  she had been portrayed as demanding or a  diva in the press she also singled out  parker's behavior is that i think she  could have been nicer  i really think she could have been nicer  i don't know what her issue is tensions  escalated later when after a death in  the family catrol posted a message on  her instagram directed at parker it read  your continuous reaching out is a  painful reminder of how cruel you really  were then and now let me make this very  clear if i haven't already you are not  my family you are not my friend so i'm  writing to tell you one last time to  stop exploiting our tragedy in order to  restore your nice girl persona at the  same time parker has maintained that she  never had it out for control saying to  elle  i don't think anybody wants to believe  that i love kim i adore her i wouldn't  have done the movie without her  one of meryl streep's first starring  roles was alongside another current  veteran dustin hoffman in 1979's kramer  vs kramer ann streep claimed to the new  york times that hoffman went too far  while filming the incident happened  during a scene in which hoffman's  character slapped strips and apparently  the slap was a little too real referring  to the scene streep said  this is tricky because when you're an  actor you're in a scene you have to feel  free i'm sure that i have inadvertently  hurt people in physical scenes but this  was my first movie and it was my first  take in my first movie and he just  slapped me and you see it in the movie  for hoffman's part he did admit that he  was difficult to work with during the  production and that his problems in his  personal life affected his co-workers on  set  although they teamed up on screen jim  carrey and tommy lee jones weren't quite  partners in crime on the set of 1995's  batman forever and much of that  animosity came from jones according to  carrie there was one incident that spoke  to jones feelings about him during an  appearance on the late norm mcdonald's  talk show carrie explained that during a  day off while filming the movie the two  happened to be sitting in the same  restaurant carrie decided to go over and  say hello which apparently wasn't  something jones wanted he went like to  hug me and said i  hate you  i really  don't like you carrie then asked what  the problem was and said i pulled up a  chair which probably wasn't smart and he  said i cannot sanction your buffoonery  of course as the riddler carries  character came with a certain amount of  buffoonery but apparently the man behind  the green question marked jumpsuit had a  little too much silliness on set for  jones's liking  marlon brando and sophia loren starred  alongside each other in the 1967 charlie  chaplin directed comedy a countess from  hong kong according to loren brando got  a bit too touchy-feely and she responded  by letting him know that was not okay  she explained in her autobiography  yesterday today tomorrow my life writing  all of a sudden he put his hands on me i  turned in all tranquility and blew in  his face like a cat stroked the wrong  way and said don't you ever dare to do  that again never again although brando  didn't do anything like that again while  filming the movie it made the rest of  the production uncomfortable for loren  she admitted that it was difficult to  work with him afterwards  gene kelly's singing in the rain co-star  debbie reynolds revealed that the  twosome's working relationship was more  fraught than their on-screen report she  wrote in her memoir he came to  rehearsals and criticized everything i  did and never gave me a word of  encouragement reynolds continued that  when it was time to shoot the kissing  scenes with kelly things got even more  uncomfortable writing  gene took me tightly in his arms and  shoved his tongue down my throat oh what  was that i screeched breaking free of  his grasp and spitting and to make  matters a bit more awkward reynolds was  just 19 at the time while kelly was 37.  reynolds went on to write i was an  innocent kid who had never been french  kissed it felt like an assault  behind the scenes of 1983's terms of  endearment there were rumors about how  tension between shirley maclaine and  deborah winger manifested on set in some  very strange ways during an appearance  on watch what happens live winger was  asked about rumors that she tried to  pass gas towards mclean or that she  licked her leg while the latter was  trying to film a love scene with jack  nicholson was any of that true you mean  you want to just go in there and say is  there something true in there yeah  there's something true despite the  fighting the duo of acting great still  holds each other in high regard at least  professionally with winger telling the  new york times i can't deny that we  fought but i think there was always a  respect between the two of us the grudge  match between hollywood icons betty  davis and joan crawford is so legendary  that it was turned into a tv show in  2017 aptly titled feud betty and joan so  what was the issue well a lot of things  the two reportedly fought over nearly  everything including lovers movie roles  fame and parenting all before ever  working together it all came to a head  when the duo start alongside each other  in 1962's whatever happened to baby jane  entertainment weekly writes that davis  once said  the best time i ever had with joan  crawford was when i pushed her down the  stairs in a scene in which davis was  supposed to fake kick crawford in the  head she actually did make contact and  it resulted in three stitches but  crawford got her revenge during a scene  where davis had to pull her out of bed  crawford secretly wore a heavy  weightlifter's belt under her costume  knowing that davis had a bad back  even when crawford died in 1977 of a  heart attack the fight lived on upon  hearing of her rival's passing davis  allegedly said you should never say bad  things about the dead only good joan  crawford is dead  good  kenny baker and anthony daniels better  known as their iconic characters r2d2  and c3po respectively weren't as close  as their iconic on-screen bond made it  seem baker has publicly said that  daniels disrespected him on set by  calling him insulting names daniels  responded to the claims telling his side  of the story in 2019 to the daily  express saying kenny decided that he  wanted to say unkind unpleasant rude  hurtful things it got worse and worse  when the suits came on however it was  all business and easy to put aside their  differences daniels explained the fact  is we didn't really appear or interact  together he was in a box he couldn't do  anything with he couldn't hear me he  never made a sound  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite on-screen partners are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

